ciary  being outraged by this do you know for  sure or have any sense that it is  encouraging some review of the process  in other cities around the country I  really have no idea except of course the  reform there the bar the organized bar  has become increasingly concerned with  ethics appearances and I think it's  probably having an effect everywhere but  I don't really have any first-hand  knowledge of what's going on anywhere  except in Chicago if you and James - it  could write an epilogue to grey law in a  few years from now what would you hope  that would be I would I would hope that  we could find more heroes I would hope  that we could that we could find someone  who would be the hero of the sequel I'd  I'd like to find at least one good  honest person in the system to make a  hero and unfortunately we didn't have  that this time that we'll have to wait  for the sequel and in addition to that  ultimately that the system will be  reformed as well or have you given up  hope on that well I would hope that the  system would be reformed and that that's  why we would have a hero who finally  brought this about what did you learn by  writing the book anything yes you always  learn things when even if you before you  actually start writing something it  helps you know clarify the thought  process that's why I see sometimes  courts issue decisions and say that a  written opinion will follow I think that  that's wrong because I think the writing  process is what clarifies that opinion  and the thought process and you in the  writing process you run against problems  that hadn't occurred to you or that you  hadn't focused on quite as well and you  learn a great deal and I think that at  one point it just really dawned on me  how thoroughly corrupt this entire  system was I mean we had judges who were  popping off the bench to take payoffs in  the middle of trials we had in one case  a lawyer who was literally involved and  if you invited him to dinner at your  house 